<h2 id='what-is-esignly'>🖊️ What Is Esignly?</h2>

<p>Esignly is a cloud-based electronic signature platform founded to give businesses of every size a legally compliant alternative to DocuSign and Adobe Sign without the enterprise price tag. It supports ESIGN Act and eIDAS compliance, meaning signatures executed on the platform hold up in U.S. and EU jurisdictions — a non-negotiable for luxury retailers whose consignment partners and private clients are often international.</p>

<p>The platform handles document preparation, multi-party signing sequences, audit trails, and template libraries. What separates it from generic e-sign tools is a workflow builder flexible enough to handle the kind of conditional, multi-signatory documents that show up constantly in luxury retail: a consignment agreement where the consignor, the store manager, and the insurer all need to sign in sequence, or an appraisal report that requires both the gemologist's certification and the client's acknowledgment before a piece leaves the counter.</p>

<p>Esignly integrates with Google Drive, Dropbox, and major CRMs via Zapier, so it slots into existing luxury retail tech stacks without requiring a rebuild. For operators already using platforms like <a href='https://luxeretailstack.com/reviews/salesforce-for-luxury-retail'>Salesforce for luxury retail</a>, the Zapier bridge means signed documents flow directly into client records.</p>

